@startuml transient-vs-sustained
title US-04: Transient vs Sustained - Single OUT_OF_RANGE Does Not Alert, Sustained Deviation Does

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\ndeviation.candidates" as DevCandKafka
participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
database "Redis\ndeviation-counter:{id}" as DevState
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka

== Transient OUT_OF_RANGE event (no alert) ==

DevCandKafka -> Evaluator : { entity_id: DEF, status: OUT_OF_RANGE,\n  deviation_metres: 45000 }

Evaluator -> DevState : INCR deviation-counter:DEF
DevState --> Evaluator : counter = 1

Evaluator -> Evaluator : counter < DEVIATION_SUSTAINED_PINGS\nno alert emitted

note over Evaluator
  A single OUT_OF_RANGE event could be
  a GPS glitch or brief correction.
  Not actionable on its own.
end note

== BACK_IN_RANGE event - counter reset ==

DevCandKafka -> Evaluator : { entity_id: DEF, status: BACK_IN_RANGE }

Evaluator -> DevState : DEL deviation-counter:DEF
note over Evaluator
  Counter reset. Transient - no alert raised.
  Deviation Detector observed entity return
  to within baseline threshold.
end note

== Sustained deviation (N consecutive OUT_OF_RANGE events) ==

loop for N consecutive OUT_OF_RANGE events
  DevCandKafka -> Evaluator : { entity_id: DEF, status: OUT_OF_RANGE,\n  deviation_metres: 45000 }
  Evaluator -> DevState : INCR deviation-counter:DEF
end

DevState --> Evaluator : counter >= DEVIATION_SUSTAINED_PINGS

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish ROUTE_DEVIATION alert\n{ entity_id, current_position,\n  baseline_position, deviation_metres,\n  sustained_cycles }

@enduml
